      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;row entry__media&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;column xl-12&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;figure class=&#34;featured-image&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;img src=&#34;https://images.pexels.com/photos/4578660/pexels-photo-4578660.jpeg&#34; sizes=&#34;2400px&#34; alt=&#34;Machine Learning&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt; &#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;introduction&#34;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this project, I set out to explore image similarity using deep learning. Leveraging the power of Keras, I aimed to detect similarities between images using a Pokémon image dataset from Kaggle. The idea was simple: take a pre-trained ResNet50 model, process Pokémon images into their vector forms, and then compare these vectors with an image of myself. The results? You&amp;rsquo;ll see soon enough.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
